  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "IEEE1905: fix IPv6 type TLV (with no other addresses) parsing",
  "description": "Current Wireshark version fails to parse Ieee1905 IPv6 Type TLV when \"Number of Other IPv6 addresses\" is 0:\n![image](/uploads/a445c27c286176346643c2997c6c4d21/image.png){width=900 height=182}\n\nThis bug is caused by the missing `entry_index` increment when `continue`-ing a loop.\nYou can actually even see two \"IPv6 type 0 info\" records, both having 0 index.\n\nWith this fix Wireshark correctly parses this packet:\n![image](/uploads/550840d518685b61877bda5795cff5d4/image.png){width=900 height=173}\n\nProblematic PCAP file is attached:\n[demo.pcapng](/uploads/67f1ea797cf3565cc581f5ce59671a28/demo.pcapng)",
